WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.267
Following all the breaking

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.002
news right now

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:02.802
in the fatal police

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:05.305
beating of Tyre Nichols in Memphis.

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:07.440
And that includes the new revelation

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.641
that a seventh police

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:09.542
officer involved in

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:12.112
Nichols arrest has been relieved of duty.

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:13.179
Let's bring in

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:15.215
CNN this morning, anchor Don Lemon,

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:17.550
along with CNN legal analyst Joey Jackson

00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:18.785
and the former president

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.787
and CEO of the NAACP,

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:21.988
Cornell William Brooks.

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:24.090
Guys, thanks very much for joining us.

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:26.126
Don, I know you've just returned

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:29.095
from Memphis as we learn that more police

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:31.664
and fire personnel, EMTs for that matter,

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:33.033
have now been fired.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.200
What's your sense

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.402
from local officials

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:36.870
that you spent days there?

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:37.771
Will we continue

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:38.938
to see those

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:41.274
who were at the scene face consequences?

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:43.176
Shocking that this all happened.

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:45.345
First of all, not so surprising,

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:46.780
quite honestly, that this is happening.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:49.115
They are doing exactly what they said

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:50.183
that they were going to do.

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:51.751
And I think every member of this panel

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:52.652
will agree.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:53.153
The police

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:54.921
chief told me in that interview

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:55.488
on Friday

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:57.557
morning that there could be more charges

00:00:57.557 --> 00:00:59.325
and more people involved.

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:00.360
The district attorney

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.462
said the same thing on Thursday

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:03.430
afternoon.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:05.532
So it's not surprising

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:07.133
that this is happening.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.768
But the speed

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:10.470
with which this is happening,

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.605
I think is remarkable.

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:13.306
It was five

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:14.908
the five initial officers,

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:16.042
they prioritized it.

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:18.211
They realized they had to do something

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:20.146
And then as they go through the video,

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:23.550
we saw the sheriff's deputy on Friday.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:26.519
His superior had just seen the video.

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:27.053
And therefore,

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:29.355
he was under investigation.

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:31.024
And then now you have the two officers.

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:32.759
It was six earlier in the day.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:33.760
Now it is seven.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:35.595
The five initial officers and the two

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:37.397
the last two are relieved of duty.

00:01:37.397 --> 00:01:39.199
Pending an administrative hearing.

00:01:39.199 --> 00:01:40.633
They are not fired.

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:43.203
So, yeah. Will there be more?

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:43.970
Probably.

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:46.206
And I

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:47.040
think, again, they're

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.241
doing exactly what they said

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:49.042
they're going to do.

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:50.043
And they're more charges

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:52.078
and more people will probably

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:54.347
be there will be a fallout from for them.

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:57.717
Joey, let me get your thoughts go ahead.

00:01:58.151 --> 00:01:59.953
Yeah, Wolf, I certainly believe that.

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:00.954
Listen, accountability

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:02.088
comes in many forms.

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:03.089
And the reality

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:04.524
is, is that each and every person

00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:05.158
who was there,

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:06.092
who enabled

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.227
who assisted

00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:09.729
who participated, who did nothing.

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:11.431
Everyone has a responsibility.

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:13.166
The world is watching. Who are we?

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:14.467
Who are they?

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:15.502
As a unit

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:16.870
and as police officials

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:18.605
it's about courtesy, professionalism

00:02:18.605 --> 00:02:19.205
and respect.

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:21.241
Was any of that shown to Mr. Nichols?

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:22.308
Of course not.

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:23.543
And so clearly,

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:25.044
as the investigation continues,

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:26.479
I think you'll see more fallout

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:27.680
and with that, Wolf,

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.582
I understand that there's many forms

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:30.717
of legal accountability.

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:32.118
One, of course, is criminal.

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:33.720
And I think they should be examined.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.155
Everyone should be examined

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:37.490
for either acting or failing to act.

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:38.191
That's number one.

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:39.659
Number two, administrative.

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:40.793
Did you do your job?

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:41.794
Did you do it properly?

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:42.295
Did you do it

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:43.463
in accordance with policies,

00:02:43.463 --> 00:02:44.797
rules, regulations, procedures?

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:46.566
If no, you shouldn't be there.

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:47.800
You should not be privileged

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.302
or entitled to have that job.

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:49.636
And then,

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:49.969
of course,

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:51.271
there's a civil component

00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:52.238
and civil component

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:54.440
designed monetarily to punish family

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:57.243
once their son not money their son.

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:59.045
But the law recognizes

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:00.947
that not only with respect to money,

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:02.682
but with regard to the reforms

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:04.684
that come about as a result of a lawsuit.

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:05.852
So without question,

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:06.986
this is accountability

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:08.521
that's very important to Memphis

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:10.523
and throughout the country.

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:12.392
Cornell, give me your thoughts, too.

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:14.727
Absolutely.

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:15.295
Here we have a

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:15.862
situation

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:17.797
where you have a bystander effect

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:18.665
in blue.

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:19.399
In other words,

00:03:19.399 --> 00:03:20.667
you have people with the duty

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:22.602
and responsibility to act

00:03:22.602 --> 00:03:23.203
who are charged

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:25.171
with the responsibility of acting,

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:26.906
but they choose not to act.

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:29.042
So there's a kind of collective paralysis

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:30.610
that makes bad worse.

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:31.110
In other words,

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.379
someone who stays and beaten

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:35.014
and pepper sprayed,

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:38.218
who is essentially watched over by those

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:39.519
with a duty of care.

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:40.153
In other words,

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:41.688
they're charged with the responsibility

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:43.022
of looking out for this young man

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:44.791
and failed to do so.

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:45.425
You know, Don,

00:03:45.425 --> 00:03:47.393
you spent days and days there in Memphis.

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:47.760
What is it

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:48.661
going to take

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:50.797
to stop this kind of deadly incident

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:52.532
from happening in the first place?

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:53.900
What did you learn there?

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.201
Well, I think it's accountability

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:56.769
and not just accountability.

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:58.471
And in the way that you it,

00:03:58.471 --> 00:03:59.472
I would be interested to know

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:00.440
what these two gentlemen think,

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.442
but I think people there want to know.

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:04.010
Okay, so they were fired, right?

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:04.978
And they'll face

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:06.279
whatever legal consequences

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:07.213
they will face.

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:09.249
But I think they many people believe

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:10.850
that going into this

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.852
before these incidents happen,

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:14.220
if police can be held

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.222
personally responsible well, meaning

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:17.490
they can be sued.

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.025
Meaning there is a liability,

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:20.493
meaning they will lose money,

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:21.995
they could lose their homes.

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:23.029
And that

00:04:23.029 --> 00:04:24.330
that personal accountability

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:25.565
doesn't often happen

00:04:25.565 --> 00:04:26.499
with police departments.

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:27.900
You can sue the department

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.169
and then the taxpayer ends up

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:33.006
we end up paying for the lawsuits

00:04:33.006 --> 00:04:33.940
and the money.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.341
Perhaps if that

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:36.976
changed and police

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:38.811
were personally responsible

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:40.980
for paying victims,

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:43.483
for paying back the taxpayer and so on

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:44.150
and so forth,

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.018
that they would think

00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:46.619
about their actions in advance,

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:48.755
knowing that their families

00:04:48.755 --> 00:04:51.691
also may face ramifications for this.

00:04:52.392 --> 00:04:53.326
You know, Joey,

00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:54.160
as of right now,

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:54.827
five police

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:57.063
officers have been criminally charged.

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:58.431
That is one hurdle.

00:04:58.431 --> 00:04:59.732
But the other piece of this

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:01.434
are the actual convictions.

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:02.535
Down the road,

00:05:02.535 --> 00:05:03.836
you're a criminal defense attorney.

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:06.272
How difficult is that piece?

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:06.806
I think it's

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:08.641
very well for the following reasons.

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:09.108
When you wouldn't

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:10.443
examine a case like this,

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:11.878
you have to examine what brought

00:05:11.878 --> 00:05:13.246
about the police conduct.

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:14.881
Number one, police do not

00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:16.816
and should not be engaging in any force

00:05:16.816 --> 00:05:18.484
unless there's an immediate threat.

00:05:18.484 --> 00:05:19.719
Was there an immediate threat

00:05:19.719 --> 00:05:20.920
that any one could say

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:22.789
reasonably they saw on that video

00:05:22.789 --> 00:05:23.222
that Mr.

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:25.258
Nichols posed at the time answer no.

00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:26.492
The second question, Wolf,

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:27.894
becomes the proportionality

00:05:27.894 --> 00:05:28.795
of that conduct.

00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:30.229
Look at the blows that were thrown.

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:32.231
Look at the kicks that that they had.

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:33.366
Look at the pepper spraying.

00:05:33.366 --> 00:05:34.934
Look at the asset that was used.

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:36.102
Was that proportionate

00:05:36.102 --> 00:05:37.236
to anything that Mr.

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:38.671
Nichols was doing at the time?

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:40.073
Did he deserve any of that?

00:05:40.073 --> 00:05:41.274
Look at the reasonability

00:05:41.274 --> 00:05:43.409
of their conduct collectively now.

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:44.577
And that of course, police.

00:05:44.577 --> 00:05:45.945
Very briefly, each.

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:46.813
Each individual

00:05:46.813 --> 00:05:47.747
defendant will say, well,

00:05:47.747 --> 00:05:48.481
I only kicked him.

00:05:48.481 --> 00:05:49.182
I only punched him.

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:50.717
I only did whatever I did.

00:05:50.717 --> 00:05:51.718
It's not only that.

00:05:51.718 --> 00:05:52.051
Well,

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:53.853
you have to examine it in the context

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:55.421
of what everyone else was doing.

00:05:55.421 --> 00:05:57.056
You didn't reasonably know

00:05:57.056 --> 00:05:58.591
that if you would engage in the conduct

00:05:58.591 --> 00:05:59.225
you engaged

00:05:59.225 --> 00:06:00.326
in, in keeping with what

00:06:00.326 --> 00:06:01.527
everyone else was doing,

00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:03.429
that he could die as a result of that.

00:06:03.429 --> 00:06:04.163
Really

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:07.200
So that puts a very high responsibility

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:07.800
on the defense.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:08.601
Last point,

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:10.269
and that is the inactivity

00:06:10.269 --> 00:06:11.637
that we all talked about.

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:12.839
You're there to protect.

00:06:12.839 --> 00:06:13.740
You're there to serve.

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:15.608
You there to preserve life, liberty.

00:06:15.608 --> 00:06:16.609
And you didn't do it.

00:06:16.609 --> 00:06:18.444
And so the failing to act also.

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:19.245
So it's a

00:06:19.245 --> 00:06:21.180
it creates a very difficult environment

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:23.282
for a defense in this particular case.

00:06:23.316 --> 00:06:23.716
Cornell,

00:06:23.716 --> 00:06:25.118
I know you wanted to make a point

00:06:25.118 --> 00:06:26.652
just a few moments ago, but go ahead.

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:28.354
Sure.

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:29.222
I think one of the things

00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:30.590
that's really important

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:30.890
for us

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:33.292
to appreciate here is for ordinary people

00:06:33.292 --> 00:06:35.161
that say people are not lawyers.

00:06:35.161 --> 00:06:35.895
Accountability

00:06:35.895 --> 00:06:37.430
means more than a conviction.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:38.264
Accountability.

00:06:38.264 --> 00:06:38.965
Accountability

00:06:38.965 --> 00:06:41.000
means more than a monetary payment,

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:43.202
meaning we're able to sue

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:44.570
a law enforcement officers

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:46.806
in the absence of qualified immunity.

00:06:46.806 --> 00:06:47.640
Accountability

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:50.209
means that you can walk down the street

00:06:50.777 --> 00:06:52.111
and have your body

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:53.746
and your being be intact.

00:06:53.746 --> 00:06:54.680
So in other words,

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:55.281
what Tyre

00:06:55.281 --> 00:06:56.416
Nichols mother

00:06:56.416 --> 00:06:57.784
accountability means that

00:06:57.784 --> 00:06:59.185
her son would be alive.

00:06:59.185 --> 00:07:00.853
So we need to be very clear about this.

00:07:00.853 --> 00:07:02.989
Conviction is not resurrection.

00:07:02.989 --> 00:07:05.491
Her boy is not coming back.

00:07:05.658 --> 00:07:07.093
Cornell, William Brooks,

00:07:07.093 --> 00:07:08.561
Don Lemon, Joey Jackson, guys,

00:07:08.561 --> 00:07:09.896
thank you very, very much.

00:07:09.896 --> 00:07:10.663
We'll stay on top of this

00:07:10.663 --> 00:07:11.464
story, to be sure.

